„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8of judgment, because the prince of this world is judged.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDI have yet many things to say unto you, but ye cannot bear them now.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËHowbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth: for he shall not speak of himself; but whatsoever he shall hear, that shall he speak: and he will shew you things to come.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNHe shall glorify me: for he shall receive of mine, and shall shew it unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAll things that the Father hath are mine: therefore said I, that he shall take of mine, and shall shew it unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtA little while, and ye shall not see me: and again, a little while, and ye shall see me, because I go to the Father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÏThen said some of his disciples among themselves, What is this that he saith unto us, A little while, and ye shall not see me: and again, a little while, and ye shall see me: and, Because I go to the Father?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^They said therefore, What is this that he saith, A little while? we cannot tell what he saith.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎNow Jesus knew that they were desirous to ask him, and said unto them, Do ye enquire among yourselves of that I said, A little while, and ye shall not see me: and again, a little while, and ye shall see me?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ Verily, verily, I say unto you, That ye shall weep and lament, but the world shall rejoice: and ye shall be sorrowful, but your sorrow shall be turned into joy.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃA woman when she is in travail hath sorrow, because her hour is come: but as soon as she is delivered of the child, she remembereth no more the anguish, for joy that a man is born into the world.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~And ye now therefore have sorrow: but I will see you again, and your heart shall rejoice, and your joy no man taketh from you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd in that day ye shall ask me nothing. Verily, verily, I say unto you, Whatsoever ye shall ask the Father in my name, he will give it you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my name: ask, and ye shall receive, that your joy may be full.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢These things have I spoken unto you in proverbs: but the time cometh, when I shall no more speak unto you in proverbs, but I shall shew you plainly of the Father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAt that day ye shall ask in my name: and I say not unto you, that I will pray the Father for you:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhfor the Father himself loveth you, because ye have loved me, and have believed that I came out from God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiI came forth from the Father, and am come into the world: again, I leave the world, and go to the Father.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTHis disciples said unto him, Lo, now speakest thou plainly, and speakest no proverb.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNow are we sure that thou knowest all things, and needest not that any man should ask thee: by this we believe that thou camest forth from God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ'Jesus answered them, Do ye now believe?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­Behold, the hour cometh, yea, is now come, that ye shall be scattered, every man to his own, and shall leave me alone: and yet I am not alone, because the Father is with me.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book*§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse!¦verses‘„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThese things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace. In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.¦layout ªlast_verse!